TU1NZ / WANT ME SEEN S11.2 P0 ROLLBACK BINDING

Classification: SOURCE_CONFIG_ROLLBACK_BINDING_GAP
Public impact: wantmeseen.com returned HTTP 502
Canary impact: S11 controller absent; Canary and Full remained disabled

Evidence

- Target WMS runtime emitted S10_WMS_PUBLIC_READY before rollback.
- Application and Control repositories returned to the exact clean source
  commits after rollback.
- The restored WMS copy failed the restored Application parser with
  S10_PUBLIC_COPY_KEYS_INVALID_EN.
- Contracts, bot identity, community contract, aggregate state and
  traffic-quality state validated independently.
- S10 WMS, S9 health and S10 health were RED after rollback.

Root cause

The old preflight bound repository commits but not the complete installed
runtime/configuration tuple. The backup captured a copy compatible with the
previously running in-memory code, while rollback restarted the repository
source commit. Those independently valid artifacts were not compatible as a
pair.

Recovery contract

1. Require the exact observed failed state and exact original backup.
2. Create and verify a second full backup before mutation.
3. Validate the canonical recovery copy using the exact rollback source,
   installed base contracts and both aggregate state files without binding a
   network port.
4. Install only that canonical copy and restart only public WMS.
5. Commit recovery only after public pages and health are GREEN.
6. Run S8/S9/S10 health, timer, acquisition and product-boundary gates.
7. Preserve S11 state, all latency evidence and both repository commits.
8. Do not retry S11 Canary in this recovery.
